WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.490
- And boundaries, I'm
gonna be honest with you,

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:06.420
are not my forte.
(laughing)

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:10.450
Brene, how is giving less of
your time considered generous?

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:12.850
'Cause how do I sell that to people?

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:16.600
Is my question.
(laughing)

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.500
- Okay, so this is the
weirdest part of our research.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.470
So early on, maybe 10 years in,

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:24.027
I had this stack of data and I was like,

00:00:24.027 --> 00:00:25.927
"These are the most compassionate people

00:00:25.927 --> 00:00:26.770
"I've ever come across."

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:29.150
I mean, we were interviewing like monks.

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:31.430
We were interviewing really
compassionate people.

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:32.950
And so we asked ourselves,

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:35.130
what are these folks have in common?

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:37.940
And I mean, we're talking
about close to 500,000 pieces

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:39.390
of data over 20 years now.

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:40.940
And we're like, what are the,

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:43.360
and I thought the answer
was gonna be spirituality.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:46.700
Like compassionate people
have spirituality in common.

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:47.550
But I was wrong.

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:50.200
The answer is the most
compassionate people

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:51.760
that we have interviewed and studied

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:55.002
in the last 20 years,
are the most boundaried.

00:00:55.002 --> 00:00:59.150
And so what I've learned
is that boundaries are not

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:01.010
you know, someone who
studies vulnerability,

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:03.840
I would say boundaries are not a wall

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.100
or a moat around your heart.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.430
They are the path to self-respect.

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:12.450
Boundaries are saying
that I choose self-love

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:15.210
and self-respect over what you think

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:18.091
of me or the possibility
of disappointing you.

00:01:18.091 --> 00:01:20.410
And how this ties to generosity

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:22.070
and the research is really interesting.

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:26.570
And here's the thing,
we're not generous and kind

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:29.483
to people who are walking all over us.

